{"assumptions":["ASM-1 and ASM-13: the system has no migrated employee, assignment, or vehicle records at startup; administrators enter existing records, with seed data available for setup.","ASM-2 and ASM-14 conflict on release dates. This spec permits releases for any date, while the configured Folio3 work calendar defines working days for default dedicated use and utilization reporting.","ASM-3, ASM-17, and ASM-18: the app integrates with Folio3-selected LPR and indicator equipment; verification failure leaves the indicator inactive and security follows the existing escalation procedure.","Q-1 and ASM-4: Security Guards use only the entrance indicator and existing sticker process; the web app has no guard-facing screen.","ASM-5 and ASM-19: employee availability notifications use fixed-template email only, not native push or SMS.","ASM-6: utilization records have on-screen filters and CSV export, with no custom report builder.","ASM-7 and ASM-22: interfaces use English, left-to-right text.","ASM-9 and ASM-24: supported browsers are the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.","ASM-10 and ASM-25: parking operations require an internet connection.","ASM-11: employees may add and edit their own vehicle plates, and administrators may also manage vehicle records; vehicle make, model, and color are optional.","ASM-12: an existing administrator assigns and removes administrator and Security Guard roles in the web app.","ASM-15: the Folio3 office local time zone governs release times, parking-day boundaries, and report scheduling.","ASM-16: administrators configure space counts by floor; allocation tracks counts and returns an assigned floor.","ASM-20: the weekly overall utilization percentage is 100 times used eligible allocations divided by eligible allocations in that reporting week; eligible allocations are dedicated allocations not released plus confirmed temporary claims, and used allocations have at least one registered vehicle entry that day; the value is 0 percent when there are no eligible allocations.","ASM-21 does not specify an exact Monday send time; the report job runs Monday morning in the Folio3 office time zone.","ASM-23 supersedes the conflicting default in ASM-8: no formal WCAG conformance target is assumed beyond responsive, touch-operable controls.","ASM-26: first-year scale is up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records.","ASM-27: hosting is in one cloud region in the client's cloud account."],"critic":[{"finding":"2 — AC-17.3 only records an unsuccessful set-inactive request when the indicator integration is unavailable, so the spec neither ensures the green indicator becomes inactive nor defines a retry or safe fallback despite requiring inactivity on every verification failure.","reqId":"REQ-17","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"1 — REQ-19 creates utilization events for configured working days, but REQ-20 calculates the weekly denominator across the Monday-through-Sunday reporting week without excluding non-working days, so the reported percentage can include allocations with no corresponding utilization event.","reqId":"REQ-20","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"3 — AC-15.1 requires processing a recorded stickered-vehicle arrival, but no requirement defines a public interface or event source that records that arrival, leaving this acceptance criterion untestable at the specified app surface.","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"2 — AC-3.2 tests an active employee saving a vehicle but never verifies that the employee can only add or edit their own plates, leaving the assumed self-service vehicle flow without an observable authorization boundary for employee vehicle data.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"2 — REQ-18 requires recording every unsuccessful entrance-verification attempt, but its acceptance criterion covers only a verification that succeeds or fails after processing and does not establish audit records for rejected unauthenticated or replayed requests described in REQ-16.","reqId":"REQ-18","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"}],"lint":[{"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L9 size","details":"This spec has 24 requirements, about 2 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.","passed":false},{"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","passed":true}],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"At viewport widths 320, 768, 1024, 1440, and 1920 CSS pixels: zero horizontal page overflow; primary touch targets are at least 44 × 44 CSS pixels.","text":"Responsive employee and administrator pages must remain usable across phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized primary controls."}],"outOfScope":["Native iOS and Android clients and app-store distribution; the requested phone workflows are delivered in the responsive web app.","Push and SMS notifications; availability notifications use email under ASM-5 and ASM-19.","A Security Guard sign-in or guard-specific web workflow; guards rely on the entrance indicator and existing sticker process (Q-1, ASM-4).","Offline parking operations (ASM-10, ASM-25).","A custom report builder (ASM-6)."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Google OAuth callback has a valid Google-issued ID token signature, issuer, and audience, a valid OAuth state, and an account belonging to an active Folio3 employee","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response contains an authenticated session field","when":"The callback is submitted"},{"given":"A Google OAuth callback contains a personal Gmail identity, a non-Folio3 identity, or an inactive employee identity","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and no authenticated session is returned","when":"The callback is submitted"},{"given":"A Google OAuth callback has an invalid ID token signature, issuer, or audience, or an invalid OAuth state","id":"AC-1.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is not 200 and no authenticated session is returned","when":"The callback is submitted"}],"ears":"When a person submits a Google OAuth callback, the Folio3 Parking web app shall create an authenticated session only after validating the Google-issued ID token signature, issuer, and audience, verifying OAuth state, and confirming that the account belongs to an active Folio3 employee.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated employee has directory details and administrator-maintained assignment and vehicle records","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains the employee ID, employee name, assigned parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle fields","when":"The employee requests their profile"},{"given":"An authenticated non-administrator requests another employee's profile","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403","when":"The profile request is submitted"}],"ears":"When an employee signs in successfully, the Folio3 Parking web app shall return a profile populated with corporate-directory employee details and administrator-maintained parking assignment, floor, and registered-vehicle records where present.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active employee has no registered vehicle","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the error field identifies vehicle registration as required","when":"The employee submits a parking release or claim request"},{"given":"An active employee submits a vehicle with a license plate and optional make, model, and color","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the returned vehicle record contains the plate and submitted optional fields","when":"The employee saves the vehicle profile"}],"ears":"If an active employee has no registered vehicle, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall require registration of at least one license plate before allowing that employee to use parking release or claim operations.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-6","ASM-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The caller has the Parking Administrator role and the employee profile contains corporate-directory details","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 or 201, the returned parking or vehicle record contains the submitted values, and the corporate-directory employee details remain unchanged","when":"The caller creates or updates a parking assignment or registered-vehicle record linked to that employee"},{"given":"The caller does not have the Parking Administrator role","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and no record is changed","when":"The caller submits an employee parking-assignment or vehicle-record change"}],"ears":"Where the caller has the Parking Administrator role, the Folio3 Parking web app shall provide read-only access to corporate-directory employee details and allow creation, viewing, and updating of employee parking assignments and registered-vehicle records linked to those profiles.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1","Q-3","ASM-1","ASM-11","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The caller has the Parking Administrator role","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned configuration fields match the submitted values","when":"The caller saves release-time, floor-capacity, calendar, recipient, or role configuration"},{"given":"The caller does not have the Parking Administrator role","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the configuration record is unchanged","when":"The caller submits a configuration or role-assignment change"},{"given":"Initial setup is run with an active Folio3 account designated in deployment bootstrap configuration","id":"AC-5.3","level":"api","then":"The response contains the account's Parking Administrator role field","when":"The account requests its profile after setup"},{"given":"No designated active Folio3 account is present in deployment bootstrap configuration","id":"AC-5.4","level":"job","then":"The setup job status is blocked and no initial Parking Administrator role row exists","when":"The initial setup job runs"}],"ears":"Where deployment bootstrap configuration is used, the Folio3 Parking web app shall keep initial administrator setup incomplete until configuration supplies a designated active Folio3 account, then grant that account the initial Parking Administrator role, and allow Parking Administrators to configure the daily release time, per-floor space counts, work calendar, named report recipients, and administrator and Security Guard role assignments.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1","Q-2","ASM-12","ASM-14","ASM-16","Q-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A person opens each employee and administrator flow on phone, tablet, and desktop viewport sizes","id":"AC-6.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen shows the flow without horizontal page overflow and its primary controls can be operated by touch","when":"The person navigates the flow and uses its primary controls"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking web app shall render every employee and administrator page as a responsive web page for phone, tablet, and desktop widths with touch-sized controls on narrow viewports.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","I-3","I-4","ASM-9","ASM-24"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The caller is a dedicated parking holder whose parking is reserved for today and not yet released or claimed","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and exactly one release row exists for the holder and date","when":"The caller submits a release request"},{"given":"A dedicated holder opens today's parking screen with no existing release","id":"AC-7.2","level":"manual","then":"The screen shows the parking status as Released","when":"The holder uses the release control once"}],"ears":"When a dedicated parking holder submits today's release before that parking has been released or claimed, the Folio3 Parking web app shall record one release for that holder and date from a single user action.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A dedicated holder submits a same-day release before the configured daily release time","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"The response from the availability request includes the released allocation and its status field is claimable","when":"The daily release time is reached in the Folio3 office time zone"},{"given":"A dedicated holder submits a same-day release after the configured daily release time","id":"AC-8.2","level":"api","then":"The response includes the released allocation immediately","when":"An eligible employee requests availability"},{"given":"A dedicated assignment has no release for the current working day","id":"AC-8.3","level":"api","then":"The response status field is Reserved","when":"The holder requests parking status"}],"ears":"While a dedicated assignment is expected to be used on a configured working day, the Folio3 Parking web app shall show Reserved by default and make a same-day release claimable at the configured daily release time if submitted earlier, or immediately if submitted later.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-2","ASM-14","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A dedicated holder submits one or more selected dates within the next 30 days","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the returned list contains a release record for each selected date","when":"The holder saves the schedule"},{"given":"A dedicated holder submits a selected date more than 30 days ahead","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 and no release row is created for that date","when":"The holder saves the schedule"},{"given":"A holder has scheduled a release for a future date","id":"AC-9.3","level":"manual","then":"The screen shows the selected date and scheduled release status","when":"The holder opens the release calendar"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking web app shall accept a dedicated holder's release schedule for one or more dates no more than 30 days ahead and make each scheduled release claimable at the daily release time on its selected date.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-2","ASM-14","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A scheduled release has not been claimed","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the release row has a cancelled status","when":"Its holder submits a cancellation"},{"given":"A scheduled release has already been claimed","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the claim row remains unchanged","when":"Its holder submits a cancellation"}],"ears":"If a scheduled release has not been claimed, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall allow its holder to cancel it and reject cancellation after it has been claimed while preserving the claim.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active employee has no dedicated assignment and at least one registered vehicle","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains a count field and a list of claimable released allocations","when":"The employee requests parking availability"},{"given":"An employee is inactive, has a dedicated assignment, or has no registered vehicle","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 or 409 and no claim row is created","when":"The employee requests or attempts to claim availability"},{"given":"An eligible employee opens the parking availability page","id":"AC-11.3","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays the current number of available parking spaces","when":"The page finishes loading"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking web app shall expose claimable parking availability to active Folio3 employees who have no dedicated assignment and at least one registered vehicle, including the current available-space count.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-6","ASM-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Two eligible employees submit claims for the same last available release concurrently","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"Exactly one response reports success, exactly one claim row exists, and the other response status is 409","when":"The claims are processed"},{"given":"An eligible employee claims a released allocation","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"The response contains the assigned floor field and one claim row records the employee, date, time, and allocation","when":"The claim is accepted"}],"ears":"When eligible employees claim released parking, the Folio3 Parking web app shall assign each release to only the earliest accepted claim and return the assigned floor from configured floor capacity.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee has a confirmed temporary parking claim","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 or 409 and the claim row remains confirmed","when":"The employee submits a claim-cancellation request"}],"ears":"If a temporary parking claim is confirmed, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall prevent the claimant from cancelling that claim.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A released allocation becomes claimable and eligible employees have email addresses","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"An email message is sent to eligible employee addresses using the configured fixed template","when":"The availability event is processed"}],"ears":"When a released parking allocation becomes claimable, the Folio3 Parking web app shall send an email notification using a fixed template to eligible employees without dedicated parking who have a registered vehicle.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-5","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A temporary claim exists and a permanently stickered vehicle arrival is recorded","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"The temporary claim row remains valid and its authorization status is unchanged","when":"The arrival is processed"}],"ears":"If a permanently stickered vehicle arrives, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall leave its existing sticker process unaffected and preserve any temporary claim already made for that date, including when configured capacity is exceeded.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Trusted Folio3 LPR equipment submits an authenticated request with a unique request ID or nonce and a readable plate matching a valid temporary authorization for the current date","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"The indicator integration receives an activation call and the response status is authorized","when":"The entrance verification request is processed"},{"given":"Trusted Folio3 LPR equipment submits an authenticated request with a unique request ID or nonce and a readable plate that has no valid temporary authorization","id":"AC-16.2","level":"api","then":"The indicator receives no activation call and the response status is denied","when":"The entrance verification request is processed"},{"given":"Trusted Folio3 LPR equipment submits an authenticated request with a unique request ID or nonce for a non-car detection","id":"AC-16.3","level":"api","then":"No authorization response is returned and no indicator activation call is made","when":"The entrance event is processed"},{"given":"An entrance-verification request is not authenticated as originating from trusted Folio3 LPR equipment","id":"AC-16.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 and the indicator receives no activation call","when":"The request is submitted"},{"given":"Trusted Folio3 LPR equipment resubmits an authenticated entrance-verification request with an ID or nonce that was previously accepted","id":"AC-16.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is rejected, no indicator activation call is made, and the indicator integration receives an explicit set-inactive call","when":"The request is processed"}],"ears":"When the Folio3 LPR integration submits an entrance-verification request, the Folio3 Parking web app shall authenticate the request as originating from trusted Folio3 LPR equipment, require a unique authenticated request ID or nonce and reject any previously accepted ID or nonce, then verify a detected car's readable plate against that date's temporary parking authorizations and activate the green indicator only for a valid authorization.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-3","ASM-17","Q-10","Q-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A trusted entrance verification fails because a plate is unreadable or lacks a valid temporary authorization, and the green indicator is active while its integration is reachable","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is denied, no activation call is made, the indicator integration receives an explicit set-inactive call, and the returned indicator status field is inactive","when":"The verification request is processed"},{"given":"A trusted entrance verification cannot complete because the LPR, plate-reading service, or network integration is unavailable, while the green indicator is active and its integration is reachable","id":"AC-17.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is denied, no activation call is made, the indicator integration receives an explicit set-inactive call, and the returned indicator status field is inactive","when":"The verification request is processed"},{"given":"A trusted entrance verification fails while the indicator integration is unavailable","id":"AC-17.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is denied and the outbound set-inactive request is recorded with an error field","when":"The verification request is processed"}],"ears":"If any entrance verification fails, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall issue an explicit command to set the green indicator inactive and deny entry through the temporary-parking process.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-3","ASM-18","Q-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An entrance verification succeeds or fails","id":"AC-18.1","level":"api","then":"One verification row records the timestamp, readable plate or empty plate field, result, and entry status","when":"The verification request is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking web app shall record every successful and unsuccessful entrance verification attempt with its timestamp, plate when readable, result, and entry status.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A dedicated holder has not released a parking allocation for a configured working day and one of the holder's registered plates has an entry record","id":"AC-19.1","level":"job","then":"The utilization row records the dedicated allocation as used","when":"The daily utilization job runs"},{"given":"A dedicated holder has not released a parking allocation and none of the holder's registered plates has an entry record for a configured working day","id":"AC-19.2","level":"job","then":"The utilization row records Unused Dedicated Parking","when":"The daily utilization job runs"},{"given":"An employee has a confirmed temporary claim and none of that employee's registered plates has an entry record for that day","id":"AC-19.3","level":"job","then":"The utilization row records Unused Temporary Parking with the employee, vehicle, and date fields","when":"The daily utilization job runs"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking web app shall record daily utilization events using registered-vehicle entry records, counting an allocation as used when any vehicle registered to its employee is detected that day.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-4","Q-5","ASM-2","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The Monday-morning weekly reporting job runs with utilization and parking records available for the preceding Monday-through-Sunday reporting week","id":"AC-20.1","level":"job","then":"The report file contains unused dedicated and temporary parking lists, daily and weekly statistics, released-space and claim counts, and an overall utilization-percentage field whose value equals 100 times the count of used allocations divided by the count of eligible allocations for that week, or 0 when the eligible-allocation count is zero; eligible allocations are dedicated allocations not released plus confirmed temporary claims, and used allocations are eligible allocations with at least one registered vehicle entry that day","when":"The report is generated"}],"ears":"When the weekly reporting job runs on Monday morning in the Folio3 office time zone, the Folio3 Parking web app shall generate a report containing unused dedicated and temporary parking, daily and weekly utilization statistics, released-space and claim totals, and an overall utilization percentage calculated for the reporting week as 100 times used allocations divided by eligible allocations, or 0 percent when there are no eligible allocations.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-4","ASM-15","ASM-20","ASM-21"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A named report-recipient list contains configured addresses belonging to Parking Administrators and configured addresses belonging to other roles, and the weekly report job runs","id":"AC-21.1","level":"job","then":"Email messages are sent only to the configured recipients with the Parking Administrator role, and no email message is sent to other listed addresses or any unconfigured address","when":"The report email is sent"}],"ears":"Where a Parking Administrator has configured a named report-recipient list, the Folio3 Parking web app shall send weekly employee-identifying report emails only to configured recipients who have the Parking Administrator role, omitting all other listed addresses from delivery.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-2","Q-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Parking Administrator opens utilization records","id":"AC-22.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen shows records matching the filter and the downloaded file is a CSV containing those displayed records","when":"The administrator applies a filter and exports the displayed list"},{"given":"A caller has any role other than Parking Administrator","id":"AC-22.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403, no utilization record row is returned, and no CSV file is returned","when":"The caller requests utilization records or requests their export as CSV"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking web app shall provide filterable on-screen lists and CSV export of utilization records only to Parking Administrators, and deny both operations to callers in every other role.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-6","Q-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A release, verification attempt, or utilization event has been recorded and its retention period is governed by the Folio3 policy","id":"AC-23.1","level":"job","then":"The record remains available until the policy's applicable retention period expires","when":"The retention job processes the record"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking web app shall retain parking-release audit history, LPR verification attempts, and utilization events according to Folio3's existing records-retention policy.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","I-5","I-6","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee has an unused parking utilization record","id":"AC-24.1","level":"job","then":"No warning, suspension, or penalty event or record is created","when":"The utilization job and weekly report job process that record"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking web app shall limit Phase 1 utilization functionality to monitoring, recording, and reporting without applying automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]}],"roundTrip":{"droppedSpans":[],"inventedCapabilities":[]},"settled":[{"decision":"Should all 24 requirements proceed as one implementation run, or should scope be reduced for this run? → Approve all 24 requirements as one run.","how":"answered","kind":"lint","problem":"L9 size: This spec has 24 requirements, about 2 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.","ref":"Q-9"},{"decision":"How must an LPR verification request prove it comes from trusted Folio3 equipment before it can activate the entrance indicator? → Require the request to be authenticated as coming from trusted Folio3 LPR equipment.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"[Rubric 2] REQ-16 does not require the LPR verification request to be authenticated as coming from trusted Folio3 equipment, so a forged request matching a temporary authorization could activate the entrance indicator.","ref":"Q-10"},{"decision":"Who may view employee utilization records and export them as CSV? → Only Parking Administrators may view and export utilization records; deny access to all other roles.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"[Rubric 2] REQ-22 exposes employee utilization records and CSV export to administrators but defines no denial or access-control behavior for non-administrators, leaving sensitive employee data without a specified authorization boundary.","ref":"Q-11"},{"decision":"What should deployment do if no designated active Folio3 bootstrap account is supplied? → Do not complete administrator setup until deployment configuration supplies a designated active Folio3 account; grant that account the initial Parking Administrator role.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"[Rubric 2] REQ-5 defines initial administrator creation only when a bootstrap account is supplied and gives no behavior for setup without one, which can leave the system with no administrator able to configure or use it.","ref":"Q-12"},{"decision":"When verification fails while the green indicator may already be active, what should the system do with the indicator? → Explicitly set the green indicator inactive on every verification failure.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"[Rubric 3] REQ-17 requires the indicator to remain inactive on verification failure, but AC-17.1 checks only that no activation call is made, so it does not establish that a previously active indicator is turned off.","ref":"Q-13"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"The application will be available on both iOS and Android platforms.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Build the Folio3 Parking product as a responsive web app for phone, tablet, and desktop, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.","ref":"Q-17"},{"decision":"May the weekly report email contain employee-identifying utilization data for named recipients who are not Parking Administrators? → Send employee-identifying reports only to configured recipients who are Parking Administrators; omit other listed addresses from delivery.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-21 emails employee-identifying unused-parking/utilization data to every named recipient, but Q-11 limits viewing employee utilization records to Parking Administrators and the spec does not require report recipients to hold that role.","ref":"Q-14"},{"decision":"What validation must succeed before a Google OAuth callback can create an authenticated session? → Validate the Google-issued ID token signature, issuer, and audience; verify OAuth state; and confirm the account is an active Folio3 employee.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-1 accepts a callback containing an employee identity without requiring validation of a Google-issued token, issuer/audience, or OAuth state, so the acceptance criteria do not prevent forged callbacks from creating authenticated sessions.","ref":"Q-15"},{"decision":"What replay defense should authenticated LPR entrance-verification requests use? → Require a unique authenticated request ID or nonce and reject any ID or nonce already accepted.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-16 authenticates trusted equipment but specifies no freshness or replay defense, allowing a captured authenticated request for a currently authorized plate to be replayed to activate the entrance indicator.","ref":"Q-16"},{"decision":"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk","how":"open-risk","kind":"critic","problem":"2 — AC-17.3 only records an unsuccessful set-inactive request when the indicator integration is unavailable, so the spec neither ensures the green indicator becomes inactive nor defines a retry or safe fallback despite requiring inactivity on every verification failure."},{"decision":"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk","how":"open-risk","kind":"critic","problem":"2 — AC-3.2 tests an active employee saving a vehicle but never verifies that the employee can only add or edit their own plates, leaving the assumed self-service vehicle flow without an observable authorization boundary for employee vehicle data."}]}